# SSH allowed-signers file for verifying signed release tags.
#
# Format (one signer per line): <principal> <key-type> <base64-key>
# `principal` is a free-form label (email or handle is conventional) used only
# for display -- verification is against the key material, not the label.
#
# Add the public half of the key used with `git config user.signingkey` here
# via PR before it signs its first tag. See docs/RELEASE_SIGNING.md.
#
# EXAMPLE (replace with a real maintainer key -- this file intentionally ships
# empty of real keys, so `git verify-tag` / the release.yml GA gate fail
# closed until a maintainer key is actually added):
# maintainer@example.com ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAI...
